// 0.0.45: print shop — spend white and blue matches at the outfitter's new Print shop counter on four cosmetic coats (Oilskin Slicker 15w, Bottle-Green Duster 10w+4b, Oxblood Greatcoat 8w+6b, Plum Frock Coat 4w+10b) and four lantern skins (Copper Lamp 10w, Wrought Iron 8w+2b, Verdigris 6w+4b, Nickel Plate 8b); paid in instalments (the shop keeps what's paid against each item), the last match prints it and puts it on; wear / take off from the counter or Journal · Supplies · Wardrobe; purely visual. Coats are scripted recolours of every character's own coat on walk, idle and side-idle sheets (96 sheets, alpha byte-identical to the base); lantern skins re-case cap, rim and post only — glass, wick, bloom and pips keep the tier color. Signed-in wardrobes sync to Postgres (migration 0008 wardrobes; ownership unions, newest equip wins), guests keep theirs in the local save. qa:sprites checks every coat variant: same silhouette, coat shown in every pose, on its catalog hue, one coat per outfit (k45a).
// 0.0.46: Night markets — in each city one street is a night market for one UTC hour and rewards earned on it pay ×2. Shared and serverless: the street is drawn from the city's baked list (src/game/marketStreets.ts, bake: scripts/bake-market-streets.mts, OSM snapshot 2026-10-03) with an FNV-1a seed of city + UTC hour label (e.g. detroit|2026-10-03T10), so every walker sees the same market without the server; even hours take their draw, odd hours step past both even neighbors' streets, so it never sits on the same street two hours running and any hour is worked out from its own and its neighbors' seeds (no chain back to the epoch). Eligible streets: a named pedestrian/living/residential/unclassified/tertiary/secondary/primary street that passes isWalkableWay (walkable.ts), above ground (no tunnels or lower decks), never a freeway (no motorway/trunk/ramp stretch under that name and no freeway/expressway/service-drive name), in the walk component reachable on foot from spawn (largest walk next to spawn, so a plaza island can't strand it), at least 150 m within 1.6 km of spawn (the Lantern Run reach, clipped there), and with at least one named lamp (any mark but the outfitter) within 60 m — matches are per-walker and random, so they can't decide a shared street; instead, while a market is open every other new street match drops along it. Doubled: a lamp's trivia-card coin and its bonus matches (lucky charm, perfect blue) for named lamps on the street and blank lamps within 60 m; a spark's match; The Run / The Stack coin and matches when its lamp stands within 30 m; street matches picked up within 30 m (two). The pocket caps still hold: a market match that won't fit pays its ladder value in coin (white 30, blue 90, green 270) and a full-pocket spark pays 24 coin instead of 12. The market that counts is the one open (wall clock, UTC hour) when the trivia card was dealt or the match picked up. Not doubled: the Daily Lantern Run finish (server-checked 2 white + 1 blue), print shop prices, the bank exchange, ride payouts, boost cards, cloth tips, goals, contracts, train tickets, the mystery wheel, materials (brass/ink/vellum/schematics/ingredients); leaderboard clears still count one per trivia card, so the server's tallies are unchanged (matches live in the local save; no server pays a market reward). Map: an orange breathing glow + dotted core along the street and a lantern sign at its middle ('Night market ×2', street, time left); HUD line 'Night market · <street> · N min left · ×2' (tap to walk to its nearest stretch); Journal · Places leads with the market row (until when, its lamps, next hour's street) and tags its lamps; the lamp sight and the reward pop say 'Night market ×2' with the coin it added (k46a).
// 0.0.47: phone HUD — under 640 px wide the top button row (music, sound, Daily, Help, Satchel, Journal) sat beside the status plate and squeezed it to ~30 px (80 px before the 0.0.43 Daily button), so city/ticket/Next/Goals/Train/Daily/night-market lines were an unreadable sliver and the coin count spilled out; now the buttons sit on top as 40 px squares and the plate stacks under them at full width (288–358 px at 360–430 px), 640–1023 px keeps them side by side with icon-only buttons and a non-shrinking button row, desktop (1024 px+) unchanged; qa:hud-mobile checks the plate is 200 px+ at phone, landscape, tablet sizes. Reward pop shows the boost line ('Perfect timing · Category charm') once — it was also repeated in the toast line (k47a).
