// 0.0.50: Friend tickets — after answering a trivia card a signed-in walker can tap 'Send as a friend ticket' to share that exact card as a link (/t/<token>, native share sheet or copy link); the friend signs in (guests are prompted), gets the same card on the same 25 s wick timed by the server clock, and a right answer pays both of them +1 White match (a full pocket pays 30 coin); the sender's next load or 45 s poll lands it with a small toast naming the friend First L. Server-authoritative (migration 0009 friend_tickets / friend_ticket_days / rate_hits): the card and its answer are copied from the server's own bank and the answer never reaches the friend before they answer; no self-redemption, one redemption per ticket (the first friend to open claims it), 48 h expiry, 5 tickets and 3 rewarded redemptions per sender per UTC day, a friend pair (either direction) rewards once per UTC day (unique index), 144-bit random tokens, guests can't send, every endpoint rate-limited (k50a).
