// 0.0.52: phone lamp-card polish — under 640 px the map's +/- zoom hides while the lamp card is open (it sat on the card's top-left corner, over the lamp); the card's Leave lamp / Forfeit button lives in a footer that never scrolls, and on short phones (height 880 px or less) the six fields are a 2x3 grid of names (blurb on hover/title), so at 360x780 and 390x844 the lamp, the fields and Leave lamp all fit without scrolling; the bottom-right lamp card's kicker wraps to two lines on phones instead of cutting to 'WHITE · …'; Nashville walks start on Broadway in front of Robert's Western World (new City.start; spawn still anchors the Daily Lantern Run, night-market and street bakes), so a new walker's first card is a lamp, not the Lower Broad Tailor. Trivia choices on iPhone: one answer button could look lit (lighter fill and border) before any tap — not an answer leak (every choice had the same markup; the lit one was whichever sat under the last tap, right or wrong) but iOS Safari's sticky :hover from the field tap; choice/field/ride-game hover styles now only apply under @media (hover: hover), choices render through game/choiceMarkup.ts (same class for all, keyed per card so each card mounts fresh buttons), any focused button is blurred when a card opens, and choiceMarkup.test.ts checks the choices differ only by text before the answer. Desktop unchanged (k52a).
// 0.0.53: trivia answers live on the server — the bank (banks/*, trivia.ts) and the 62 door quizzes (moved out of data.ts into server-only doorQuizzes.ts) are no longer in the browser bundle. A lamp asks the server for a card (triviaApi.dealTrivia): the server picks it with the same picker (the save's seen ids for anti-repeat, tier/rarity ladder and weekly retune, place topics and door quizzes, city-tagged cards, Run/Stack difficulty steps) and returns the prompt and server-shuffled choices with a public card id (sha256 of prompt + sorted choices — the old fnv1a(prompt + answer) id could be brute-forced to the answer) and a signed pending-card token (HMAC, stateless, no migration). The answer goes back as the chosen text (gradeTrivia); the server grades it on its own clock (the client's stopwatch, never more than 1.2 s faster than the server saw, so perfect timing can't be faked; past the wick + 2.5 s is a timeout), and only then reveals the answer and fact. For a signed-in walker the server writes the plate event and, on a right answer, the +1 rolls clear itself — the client-callable reportCorrect/reportPlate are gone; a token grades once (replays get the first result and credit nothing). Guests play on an anonymous token; the wick starts when the card arrives; nothing is spent if the card office can't be reached. Friend tickets resolve public ids. qa:no-answers fails the gate if a card prompt, a known answer or an answer key is in the built client (k53a).
