// 0.0.72: the journal and the satchel keep the record. Hiring, printing, paint, the morning crate, the match exchange, contracts, quest turn-in, and the daily blitz are done on the street — the outfitter, a ward counter, and a notice board in every city (k72a).
// 0.0.73: Help lists what each color of lamp pays — coin from a slow answer to a perfect one, paint odds, brass, stock, schematic, and how long it stays dark. The numbers are the lamp's own payout. Once you've lit any, the row also says how many of that color this save has lit, and about how many cans that is worth (k73a).
// 0.0.74: paint drops stay rarer as the color climbs, but the top of the ladder is a find you can actually hold. White 1 in 2, then 5, 10, 20, 40, and violet 1 in 80. Prism stays 1 in 10,000. Coin is unchanged (k74a).
// 0.0.75: a hidden nudge for the rarer cans. Green through violet, and prism, stay on the posted rate until five other signed-in walkers have found that can. After that, a walker who has gone more than one standard deviation past the average those players took rolls a higher chance — one extra deviation doubles it, and it never passes four times the posted rate. The Help chart does not change. Guests stay on the posted rate. White and blue are not nudged (k75a).
// 0.0.76: a tap still walks you when you're off the street. The route joins the nearest clear street, and you cross the open ground to meet it, unless that line would step on a freeway. A dead-end curb no longer traps you: aim back down the street and you leave. Holding into the end still stops, it doesn't bounce (k76a).
// 0.0.77: build fixes on 0.0.76 — SPARK_DAY restored (the build failed without it), the off-street walk join measures its distance correctly, lamps offer Math on ~19% of visits (MATH_OFFER_KEEP 0.45 → 0.43), copy and dye tests fixed (k77a).
// 0.0.78: a signed-in walker's coins, matches and city passes live on the server (migration 0016). The grade pays them, once per token; a city unlock, the print shop, the bank and the other spends are checked there too. Each device gets one first sync, which keeps the higher of the server and that device's coins, matches and tickets, clamped (250k coins, 300 matches a tier, 2 tickets), and unions cities that player already unlocked when the id is a real city. Passes, atlas visits, craft stock, lucky, cloths and distance stay server-earned. It never lowers a counter. Five devices per player. A city pass, a survey match, a contract, a blitz step and a train ride pay only from a record the server already has. A Lantern Run pays once per city per the day that run started, and only from a finished row. A ride round is dealt by the server; the played, strong-win and perfect bonus is scored from the moves sent back, and only once play spans half the ride, never above a guest. Street matches pay from that player's city-day list, once each, only in an unlocked city, only after a walk or a deal in that city in the last few minutes, at most forty a city a day. A night-market spot pays two matches while that city's market is open on the server clock, and still counts as one of the forty. Lucky and cloth are granted only when that craft spends its cost in the same write. Tickets carry over at first sync, two at most, and a ride starts only after the server takes one. The pocket is clamped on the way out as well as the way in (250k coins, 300 matches a tier, 25 passes, 150 km, real atlas visits). A contract takes three graded lamps. A blitz step takes the card that step dealt. Guests stay on the device. A second tab still picks up the pocket (k78a).
// 0.0.79: Friday weekly trivia cards (2026-10-16) — 18 new verified cards in weekly_20261016, no math: Tucson, Austin, Temple and Denver council and election facts (partisan Tucson elections, Austin's 10-1 plan and term limits, Temple districts, Denver at-large seats, term limits and veto override), the 2026 economics Nobel (Hall and Woodford) and A'ja Wilson's record fifth WNBA MVP. Accuracy pass: 13 Oct 2 cards got plausible wrong choices in place of joke ones (a few reworded to real facts, e.g. Texas House 150 seats, London Assembly 25 members), one Temple tree card that repeated the pecan card was dropped, and the Bolsonaro card no longer gives its answer away by format (k79a).
// 0.0.80: street counters and notice boards stand on a street you can walk. The nudge that set a stand beside its lamp did not look at the map, so the Congress Newsstand in Tucson sat in the Mission Garden lawn and others landed in parks out of reach; those stands now sit on the nearest walkable street (standSpots.ts). qa:stands checks every outfitter, station, counter and board against the live walk graph (k80a).
// 0.0.81: math levelled out — 602 near-duplicate easy math cards cut (identity and zero sums, products and quotients like 0 ÷ 13 and 7 × 1, n + 1 and n − 1, x − x, the b + a twin of every a + b, and the subtraction that just undoes an addition card already in the deck), so math is 19.3% of trivia cards (was 24.2%, cap 20%). 12 new verified political cards (Canada's Supreme Court, Senate and Commons, the European Parliament, U.S. amendment ratification; L.A. council and mayor term limit; Toronto council, amalgamation and Metro Toronto; the GLA and the GLC). A blue math lamp now deals its medium blue cards as well as the easy ones (it only ever dealt the easy half). The Texas Capitol stone card no longer gives its answer away: every choice is a named Texas stone (k81a).
// 0.0.82: character polish pass — every walker stands on the street instead of floating like a sticker: a soft ground shadow under the feet, smooth scaling instead of blocky pixels, a thin dark ink edge instead of the offset halo, a small step bob and squash timed to the walk, idle breathing and a lean into side walks (reduced motion turns the motion off). Coats and dyes recolor cleanly: no more lavender chin, bib, belly or lip on the Corgi, no brown lantern sleeve, no brown specks in the coat; the reddish fringe on ears and tails is gone. qa:sprites fails coat color on fur. Sprite sheets recompressed losslessly (static 8.00 → ~6.3 MB); sprite cache stamp k81p (k82a).
// 0.0.83: the Turtle is redrawn — new painted art at 192 px frames with 8-frame walks in all four directions (true right-facing frames, not mirrors): a real stride with heel strike and push-off, the coat hem swinging with the legs, the body rising and falling, the lantern (always in its right hand) swinging; toward and away from the camera the feet step forward with hip sway. Standing still it settles into a hunched 3/4 pose that breathes, sways its lantern and blinks. Its coat is a separate layer, so print-shop coats and dyes recolor exactly the coat and never the shell, belly, skin, boots or lantern (qa:sprites proves it for every coat and dye). The other scouts keep their sheets for now; v2 sprite stamp k83a (k83a).
// 0.0.84: email + password accounts (sign up / sign in under Google and X, reset when mail is switched on); X sign-ins cannot take over a password account; sessions end at once on password reset (k84a).
