// 0.0.89: Mystery Wheel hotfix — a refused signed-in claim (server counts fewer graded answers than the device, e.g. answers before sign-in) no longer re-shows the same landed wheel forever; it closes, marks that color caught up, and a network failure retries later. The wheel card has a ✕ (Later) so nobody can be trapped. v2 sprite stamp k89a (k89a).
// 0.0.90: the morning crate opens itself on the first answer of the day (pop-up with pay and streak day), then the Daily Blitz is offered once (Play now / Later); a two-line, three-card tutorial; a ✕ beside the Route pill (and Esc) cancels the whole route; earning a train ticket no longer auto-walks you to the station; street matches doubled (18 opening, cap 16/10, spawns every 14–39s, 80 claims a city-day); an "I'm stuck" button in Help puts you back at the start with nothing lost, and a walker wedged on a route leg gives up after 3 re-plans instead of retrying forever. Walk +15%, cab +25% (walk 92→105.8, cab 184/230→230/287.5). A perfect lamp gives back its match (same tier, not violet; overflow coin if the pocket is full). Everyone gets one free city pass, once (new players start at 1) (k90a).
// 0.0.91: night markets sit on streets with 3+ lamps (best-lit fallback, named paths count, busier streets drawn more often) and their lamps relight 3x as fast; street matches only spawn on the walk you can reach from the city start (qa:street-spawns); a tap past the play area or across water (Windsor from Detroit) walks to the nearest reachable spot instead of refusing (k91a).
// 0.0.92: the Mystery Wheel v2: bright tier-colored match slices, brass coin and ink ingredient slices with icons, rim lights, a pointer that clicks on every peg, an ease-out that sails a little past and settles back, a burst and glow on the winning slice (reduced motion lands at once); new match prizes (a pair, and a rare match one tier up; violet only on a violet wheel), paid by the server too; signed in, Spin claims on the server first and the wheel lands on the slice the server paid; the Cut slice is now two half slices: Take all (every other prize on the wheel at once, server-paid) and Nothing (k92a).
// 0.0.93: answer streaks (5 in a row pays a white match, 10 a blue; server-paid), a daily match cache per city off the main roads (2-3 white/blue/green matches once a day), three daily goals replace the errand (all three pay a green match), and a Quest Board near each start with a "!" glow, a first-play arrow and a journal shortcut; the lantern result is emblems + amounts with a big rating word (count-up, pop-in, Perfect sparkles); street matches no longer pause at 7+ held (k93a).
// 0.0.94: rides cap at 8 min with a gentler distance line (median ~7 min, was ~9.5; max 8, was 11), pay table rebased to a six-minute ride and the long-haul blue at 7 min; each ride round runs a little faster (+6%/round, up to +30%) and the first round dealt past halfway is a bonus round (+10% pace, win = +2 white, server-paid); desktop rides show whole-game top-5 boards (lanterns lit right, distance walked) with your own rank pinned when off the top 5; the street map cap stays 16 until 15+ held (k94a).
// 0.0.95: the match cache always pays: a full color steps up to the next tier with room (white → blue → green → amber → red → violet), overflow coin only when every pocket is full (server-paid); the cache marker is a brass-banded crate with a lit match and a warm glow; a one-time make-up gift of 2 red matches for Amanda G. (server-paid once under gift:amanda-red-0095, note shown once); streak, cache and gift rewards now celebrate in a pop with the tier-colored match emblems, a big line ("5 in a row!"), a flame/sparkle burst and emblems flying to the pocket (static with reduced motion); purchases live on the account: the sync returns the scouts, charms and cloths the server recorded, so a hire survives logout and shows on every device (re-buying is a no-charge replay); Beth B.'s Corgi restored once (gift:bethb-corgi-0095, duplicate server purchases refunded at 9,600); a map tap replaces the route instead of queueing up to eight stops, the old line drops at once, and a red Stop chip shows during any walk; Help has a compact "Prize badges" key, and the ⚡ badge lists its boosts when tapped; the station shows a plain "How to get a city pass" card with live progress bars and a "Use pass" button, and Help explains city passes; every city has a red lantern (UT Tower in Austin and the Royal Ontario Museum in Toronto go amber → red); a night market needs a 300 m connected stretch and lights that whole stretch (k95a).
// 0.0.96: scout abilities. Raccoon (Rummager) 1 in 15 lamps also drops a blue; Tabby (Nine lives, 8,000) first miss a day keeps the streak, +1 s; Corgi (Zoomies, 12,000) walks 15% faster; Owl (Night eyes, 18,000) night market pays ×2.5 and the match cache shows from anywhere (others see it within 450 m); Plate (Shell, 24,000) 1 in 3 failed lamps refund the match; Sloth (Hang time, 20,000) +4 s, walks 10% slower; Giraffe (Long neck, 45,000) 2× reach for lamps and matches; Fox (Clever, 90,000) +10% lamp coin and one wrong option struck on red/violet (server picks it); Penguin (Belly slide, 900,000) cuts through blocks, 20% faster, +10% coin. Rolls are the server's; walk ceiling follows the fastest coat (k96a).
