// 0.0.97: hotfix — multi-stop routes are back: a tap still replaces the route, press and hold (~0.5 s, finger still) adds a stop on the end (5 stops max) with a ring + buzz; no browser menu on long-press; Guide line. Pocket rule (Ryan, amber flood): every color holds 30 (was white 6, blue 6, green 2, amber/red/violet 150; ride whites 22); a match on a full pocket is 1 overflow credit, 3 credits merge into 1 match of the next color only (white→blue→green→amber→red→violet), credits persist on the server (meta.credit, never from a client save), full violet pays violet coin, pockets already above 30 are kept; pocket shows n/3; Guide + badges updated (k97a).
// 0.0.98: levels and titles. Server-derived XP (right answers by tier, walking, daily goals, rides; fast early, slower later), level badge + XP bar in the HUD, level/title/name color on the boards, level-up pop. Rewards never add permanent power: a match per level (tier rises with level), name colors every 5, a 15-min double streak boost every 4, a match to gift a friend every 3. Titles: 3-rung ladders per trivia category at 250/1,000/2,000 right (sports/political/food/arts/nature are drafts), plus Night Owl, Hot Streak, Globetrotter, Perfectionist, Violet Hunter; pick one in the Journal. Backfilled from answer records; earlier levels set a baseline and are not paid retroactively (k98a). Celebrations (level-up pop, loot and match toasts) wait until the How to Play card, the daily card or any open sheet/modal closes. A scout the account owns on the server (bought or restored by a gift) is never charged or refused on re-buy, and a refused buy no longer rolls back a server-owned scout (Beth B.'s Corgi).
// 0.0.99 (hotfix): the pocket credit pip no longer flickers on a pickup: it shows a change once, after the server's pocket lands (a pickup the server refuses, or counts differently, used to show 1/3 then snap back). Press and hold on desktop: the click that ends a long hold is always swallowed (a hold longer than ~0.7 s used to replace the route it had just extended); Shift+click also adds a stop, and Help says so; a Longest streak top 5 (most right answers in a row, all-time best, computed on the server from every answer record, so history counts) in the Journal leaderboard and the desktop ride panel; reward pops show again on every device (0.0.98 held them while How to Play was already finished and while the daily card was itself waiting behind the reward, so tablets often never saw them); two pops in a row now show one after the other, and a pop never waits more than 4 s once no vault is open; Journal · Progress lists Recent rewards (last 20: what you got, where from, when; from your account ledger when signed in, from this device for guests); math cards now match their lamp color (white: add/subtract within 20; blue: two-digit add/subtract; green: times tables; amber: two-digit × one-digit and mixed steps; red: two-digit × two-digit and clean percents; violet: multi-step with brackets or squares; bare squares to 10² are green, 11²–15² red), with near-miss wrong answers and new generated sums for the higher colors; lantern skins actually show: the Print shop previews and the street lamps now re-case in copper, black iron, green verdigris or bright nickel (the sprites only differed in thin trim, so every skin looked the same) (k99a).
